Wraps Effect <code>class</code> Becomes a <code>@dataclass</code>. Validation is deferred by default — you call <code>validate(instance)</code> explicitly. Attribute access is locked until then. <code>def</code> / <code>async def</code> Wraps the call. Arguments and return value are validated eagerly on every invocation. Method Same as a function. Always place <code>@monk</code> below <code>@classmethod</code> / <code>@staticmethod</code>. <pre><code>from monk import monk

@monk                          # deferred — call validate(user) yourself
class User: ...

@monk(defer=False)             # eager — fails inside __post_init__
class StrictUser: ...

@monk
def process_user(...): ...     # eager — fails on every call
</code></pre>
